Figure (6.6) illustrates hits in the TPC; these hits are used to reconstruct tracks. The more hits along a track, the more accurately the track is reconstructed. Figure (6.7) shows the transverse momentum and the mass distributions when the minimum number of hits is greater than 10, 15, 20 and 25. The other cuts remained constant at relatively loose values (z vertex < 200 cm, r vertex < 25 cm, the log(dEdx/dEdxk) > 0.2 and the number of tracks < 10). We can see that as we increase the minimum number of hits per track, both the signal and the background decrease while the ratio of signal to background does not change significantly. To maximize the signal events, here we chose the minimum number of hits per track to be greater than 10 as the cut.

